@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. MOVIES API (Phase 5)

# 1.1 Create Movie
# @name createMovie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Inception",
  "description": "A thief who steals corporate secrets through the use of dream-sharing technology.",
  "genre": "Sci-Fi",
  "language": "English",
  "durationMinutes": 148,
  "releaseDate": "2010-07-16T00:00:00Z",
  "rating": 8.8,
  "posterUrl": "https://example.com/posters/inception.jpg"
}

### 1.2 Get All Movies (Paged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/movies?page=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

### 1.3 Get Movie By ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/movies/1
Accept: application/json

### 1.4 Search Movies By Title
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/movies/search?title=Inception
Accept: application/json

### 1.5 Update Movie
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/movies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Inception (Special Edition)",
  "description": "A thief who steals corporate secrets through the use of dream-sharing technology.",
  "genre": "Sci-Fi / Thriller",
  "language": "English",
  "durationMinutes": 148,
  "releaseDate": "2010-07-16T00:00:00Z",
  "rating": 9.0,
  "posterUrl": "https://example.com/posters/inception-special.jpg",
  "isActive": true
}

### 2. THEATRES API (Phase 6)

# 2.1 Create Theatre
# @name createTheatre
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/theatres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "PVR Cinemas IMAX",
  "address": "Phoenix Marketcity, Velachery",
  "city": "Chennai",
  "state": "Tamil Nadu",
  "phone": "+91-9876543210",
  "email": "chennai@pvrcinemas.com"
}

### 2.2 Get All Theatres
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/theatres
Accept: application/json

### 2.3 Get Theatre By ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/theatres/1
Accept: application/json

### 3. SCREENS API (Phase 6)

# 3.1 Create Screen
# @name createScreen
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/screens
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "theatreId": 1,
  "screenName": "Screen 1 (IMAX)",
  "totalSeats": 60,
  "screenType": "IMAX"
}

### 3.2 Get Screens by Theatre
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screens/theatre/1
Accept: application/json

### 3.3 Get Screen By ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/screens/1
Accept: application/json

### 4. SEATS API (Phase 6)

# 4.1 Bulk Create Seats for Screen 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/seats/bulk
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "screenId": 1,
  "seats": [
    { "rowLetter": "A", "columnNumber": 1, "seatType": "Regular", "price": 180.00 },
    { "rowLetter": "A", "columnNumber": 2, "seatType": "Regular", "price": 180.00 },
    { "rowLetter": "A", "columnNumber": 3, "seatType": "Regular", "price": 180.00 },
    { "rowLetter": "B", "columnNumber": 1, "seatType": "VIP", "price": 250.00 },
    { "rowLetter": "B", "columnNumber": 2, "seatType": "VIP", "price": 250.00 },
    { "rowLetter": "B", "columnNumber": 3, "seatType": "VIP", "price": 250.00 }
  ]
}

### 4.2 Get Seats by Screen
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/seats/screen/1
Accept: application/json

### 5. SHOWS API (Phase 7 - Schedules & Auto-generates ShowSeats)

# 5.1 Create Show (Automatically generates 6 ShowSeat records as 'Available')
# @name createShow
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shows
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "movieId": 1,
  "screenId": 1,
  "showDate": "2026-12-01T00:00:00Z",
  "startTime": "18:30:00",
  "basePrice": 200.00
}

### 5.2 Get All Shows
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shows
Accept: application/json

### 5.3 Get Show By ID (shows available vs total seats)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shows/1
Accept: application/json

### 5.4 Get Shows by Movie
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shows/movie/1
Accept: application/json

### 5.5 Overlap Detection Test (Should fail with 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shows
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "movieId": 1,
  "screenId": 1,
  "showDate": "2026-12-01T00:00:00Z",
  "startTime": "19:00:00",
  "basePrice": 200.00
}

### 6. BOOKINGS API (Phase 8 - Transactional Booking & Cancellation)

# 6.1 Create Booking for Seats 1 and 2 (ShowSeats updated to 'Booked')
# @name createBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "showId": 1,
  "seatIds": [1, 2],
  "customerName": "John Doe",
  "customerEmail": "john.doe@example.com",
  "customerPhone": "+91-9988776655"
}

### 6.2 Get Booking By ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/1
Accept: application/json

### 6.3 Prevent Double-Booking Test (Should fail with 400 Bad Request because seats 1 and 2 are already Booked)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "showId": 1,
  "seatIds": [1, 2],
  "customerName": "Jane Smith",
  "customerEmail": "jane.smith@example.com",
  "customerPhone": "+91-9988771122"
}

### 6.4 Cancel Booking (ShowSeats restored to 'Available', status changed to 'Cancelled')
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/1/cancel
Accept: application/json
